- Dependency `com.itextpdf:itext7-core:7.1.9` has **4** known CVEs need to be fixed:
  - [CVE-2021-43113](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gv87-q66h-4277): Command injection in itext7-core
    - **Severity**: **CRITICAL**
    - **Details**: iTextPDF in iText before 7.1.17 allows command injection via a CompareTool filename that is mishandled on the gs (aka Ghostscript) command line in GhostscriptHelper.java.
  - [CVE-2022-24197](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-c32g-2mgr-cfq7): Out-of-bounds Write in iText
    - **Severity**: **MEDIUM**
    - **Details**: iText v7.1.17 was discovered to contain a stack-based buffer overflow via the component ByteBuffer.append, which allows attackers to cause a Denial of Service (DoS) via a crafted PDF file.
  - [CVE-2022-24196](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hhh6-cm2m-3fhc): Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling in iText
    - **Severity**: **MEDIUM**
    - **Details**: iText v7.1.17 was discovered to contain an out-of-memory error via the component readStreamBytesRaw, which allows attackers to cause a Denial of Service (DoS) via a crafted PDF file.
  - [CVE-2022-24198](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8c9h-4q7g-fp7h): Out-of-bounds Read in iText
    - **Severity**: **MEDIUM**
    - **Details**: iText v7.1.17 was discovered to contain an out-of-bounds exception via the component ARCFOUREncryption.encryptARCFOUR, which allows attackers to cause a Denial of Service (DoS) via a crafted PDF file. NOTE: Vendor does not view this as a vulnerability and has not found it to be exploitable.
- Dependency `com.itextpdf:itextpdf:5.5.13.2` has **1** known CVEs need to be fixed:
  - [CVE-2021-43113](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gv87-q66h-4277): Command injection in itext7-core
    - **Severity**: **CRITICAL**
    - **Details**: iTextPDF in iText before 7.1.17 allows command injection via a CompareTool filename that is mishandled on the gs (aka Ghostscript) command line in GhostscriptHelper.java.
- Dependency `io.github.bonigarcia:webdrivermanager:5.6.2` has **1** known CVEs need to be fixed:
  - [CVE-2025-4641](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-pwm3-776c-8q7q): BoniGarcia WebDriverManager Affected By Improper Restriction of XML External Entity Reference
    - **Severity**: **CRITICAL**
    - **Details**: Improper Restriction of XML External Entity Reference vulnerability in bonigarcia webdrivermanager on Windows, MacOS, Linux (XML parsing components modules) allows Data Serialization External Entities Blowup. This vulnerability is associated with program files src/main/java/io/github/bonigarcia/wdm/WebDriverManager.java.
      
      This issue affects webdrivermanager: from 1.0.0 before 6.1.0.
